# Repos EXCLUDED from autonomous scheduling — NO autonomous runner work without
# your clear, explicit consent.
#
# Effect:
#   • The CLI task runner SKIPS any pending task whose repo is listed here on its
#     autonomous (fleet) picks. A CONSENTED run still works: `cli_task_runner.sh
#     --repo <name> --force` or `--task <id>` bypasses this list (manual = consent).
#   • `schedule plan` / `schedule_task.sh` / `push_schedule.sh` REFUSE to queue work
#     for these repos. Override for a single consented call: env SCHEDULE_CONSENT=1.
#
# One repo name per line (task-store convention = git basename). '#' lines ignored.
#
# Example:
#   client-production-app
#   do-not-touch-legacy
#
# This .example file is the fork-ready template. Copy to `schedule_ignore.txt`
# and list the repo basenames you never want auto-scheduled.
